 Plants: Community Patterns and Mechanisms.</article-title><publisher-loc>Oxford</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Blackwell Scientific Publications</publisher-name><fpage>313</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001208-Joshi1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Joshi</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Vrieling</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>The enemy release and EICA hypothesis revisited: incorporating the fundamental difference between specialist and generalist herbivores.</article-title><source>Ecology Letters</source><volume>8(7)</volume><fpage>704</fpage><lpage>714</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001208-Kennedy1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kennedy</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Naeem</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Howe</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Knops</surname><given-names>JMH</given-names></name><name><surname>Tilman</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Biodiversity as a barrier to ecological invasion.</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>417</volume><fpage>636</fpage><lpage>638</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12050662</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001208-Levine1"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Levine</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>D'Antonio</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Elton revisited: a review of evidence linking diversity and invasibility.</article-title><source>Oikos</source><volume>87</volume><fpage>15</fpage><lpage>26</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001208-Blossey1"><label>26<